@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-applypatch-semantics-strict-rfc-6902-atomic-non-mutating
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch semantics: strict RFC 6902, atomic, non-mutating"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services will use `applyPatch` to change stored and exchanged JSON, so it must follow RFC 6902 and
+never corrupt its input when a patch fails.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The document is deep-cloned (`structuredClone`) first and operations run on the clone; values taken from the patch are cloned too. Inputs are never mutated and the result shares no structure with them. A failure throws, so a patch is atomic.
+- The whole patch is validated before any operation runs. A non-array patch, a non-object operation, an unknown or missing `op`, a missing or non-string `path`/`from`, or a missing `value` throws `TypeError`. A malformed pointer throws `SyntaxError`. Extra members are ignored (RFC 6902, section 4).
+- An operation that fails (unresolvable target or parent, array index beyond the end or not matching the RFC 6901 grammar, `-` anywhere but `add`, failed `test`) throws `RangeError`.
+- `add` replaces an existing object member, inserts into arrays at `0..length` or `-`, and replaces the whole document for the empty path.
+- `remove` of the whole document (empty path) is rejected: the RFC leaves it undefined and there is no document left to return.
+- `replace` requires an existing target. `move` is a removal then an addition; moving a location onto itself is a no-op once `from` resolves, and moving into one of its own children is an error. `copy` clones the value.
+- `test` uses JSON equality: objects equal regardless of key order, arrays in order, numbers and strings by strict value, `null` only to `null`.
+- Only own properties are reached, and `__proto__` is written as an ordinary own member (via `defineProperty`), so patches cannot pollute prototypes.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers can tell a bad patch (`TypeError`/`SyntaxError`) from a patch that does not apply (`RangeError`).
+Documents must be structured-cloneable JSON; functions or other non-JSON values throw. Cloning costs
+time proportional to the document size on each call.
